Census Method or
Census Survey
Under Census Method, we will collect data from each
worker about his wages and then total of monthly
wages of all the 600 workers will be divided by 600 to
get average monthly wages.
Sampling Method or
Sampling Survey
Under Sampling Method, only few workers are selected say, 60
(This 60 is the sample) and total of monthly wages of these 60
workers is divided by 60. The average monthly wages so
obtained (of 60 workers) can reasonably be representative of
average monthly wages of 600 workers.
