Merits
Intensive study of population: It provides intensive anc in-depth information covering
many facets of the problems.
High degree of accuracy and reliability: Since every item of the population is observed
personally, it is possible to collect highly accurate and reliable information.
Suitability of the method: This method is suitable when different items of the population
are not homogeneous.
Demerits
Expensive: Since the data are obtained by observing every item of the population, it is a very
expensive method of investigation, especially in case of a large population.
Needs more time and manpower: Since a large volume of data are to be collected under census
investigation, more time and manpower are needed for its collection, analysis and interpretation.
Inapplicability: Census method cannot be applied in case of infinite population. If the study involves
destruction, as in case of testing of tyres on road, census cannot be conducted.
